{"version": "https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1", "title": "vanderoost", "home_page_url": "https://vanderoost.com/", "feed_url": "https://vanderoost.com/feed_json_created.json", "description": "I automate tech companies", "icon": null, "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "language": "en", "items": [{"id": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/08/05/levels-of-effective-makefile-cheatsheet/", "url": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/08/05/levels-of-effective-makefile-cheatsheet/", "title": "The 7 levels of highly effective Makefiles", "content_html": "Learn how to write a full-on Makefile from scratch to automate building C projects.", "image": "https://vanderoost.com/assets/images/social/articles/2026/08/05/levels-of-effective-makefile-cheatsheet.png", "date_modified": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "date_published": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "tags": null}, {"id": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/09/11/histogram-plotting-in-the-terminal/", "url": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/09/11/histogram-plotting-in-the-terminal/", "title": "Plotting histograms in the terminal", "content_html": "A simple C library for plotting histograms in the terminal.", "image": "https://vanderoost.com/assets/images/social/articles/2026/09/11/histogram-plotting-in-the-terminal.png", "date_modified": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "date_published": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "tags": null}, {"id": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/09/25/stop-using-rand/", "url": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/09/25/stop-using-rand/", "title": "Stop using rand()", "content_html": "<h1>Stop using <code>rand()</code></h1>\n<div class=\"rvo-video\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/-5NqTA-fDNQ\" title=\"Coding RNG from scratch in C\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n\n<p>In this article I will try to convince you to stop using <code>rand()</code> in your C projects,\nand write a better alternative from scratch.</p>", "image": "https://vanderoost.com/assets/images/social/articles/2026/09/25/stop-using-rand.png", "date_modified": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "date_published": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "tags": null}, {"id": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/10/02/how-floats-work/", "url": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/10/02/how-floats-work/", "title": "Hacking floats to learn how they work", "content_html": "<h1>Hacking floats to learn how they work</h1>\n<div class=\"rvo-video\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/ksumuyRAk-U\" title=\"Learn how floats work in C without reading the spec\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n\n<p>In this article I want to explore floating-point numbers (floats). Floats are a bit more\ncomplicated than integers. It's quite easy to convert a bunch of bits to an (unsigned)\ninteger, but for floats this is not trivial.</p>", "image": "https://vanderoost.com/assets/images/social/articles/2026/10/02/how-floats-work.png", "date_modified": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "date_published": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "tags": null}, {"id": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/10/09/better-random-floats/", "url": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/10/09/better-random-floats/", "title": "Generating random floats", "content_html": "<h1>Generating random floats</h1>\n<div class=\"rvo-video\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/qa83_KrkVIM\" title=\"Generating better random floats in C\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n\n<p>We've already hand-rolled our own RNG in a <a href=\"../2026-09-14_stop-using-rand/index.md\">previous\narticle</a>, to improve on what the C standard\nlibrary <code>rand()</code> gives us.</p>\n<p>We also talked about <a href=\"../2026-10-02_how-floats-work/index.md\">how floats work</a>.</p>\n<p>In this article, I want to combine the two. I want to find out how we can generate\nrandom floating-point numbers between 0 and 1, and improve our rng.c library.</p>", "image": "https://vanderoost.com/assets/images/social/articles/2026/10/09/better-random-floats.png", "date_modified": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "date_published": "2026-10-09T12:40:37+00:00", "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "tags": null}, {"id": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/09/13/why-company-ai-projects-fail/", "url": "https://vanderoost.com/articles/2026/09/13/why-company-ai-projects-fail/", "title": "Why 95% of company AI projects fail", "content_html": "<h1>Why 95% of company AI projects fail</h1>\n<p>It's an interesting time to be alive. The \"AI transformation\" is happening.</p>\n<p>Many business owners feel FOMO on AI adoption. Yet, allegedly 95% of AI projects in companies fail, according to an MIT report. Why is this?</p>\n<p>I've talked to business owners and AI automation agencies. This is what I found.</p>", "image": "https://vanderoost.com/assets/images/social/articles/2026/09/13/why-company-ai-projects-fail.png", "date_modified": "2026-09-13T00:00:00+00:00", "date_published": "2026-09-13T00:00:00+00:00", "authors": [{"name": "Richard van der Oost"}], "tags": null}]}